# Local scratch
tmp/

# openapi-generator-cli: auto-created on `pnpm dlx openapi-generator-cli` runs
# (e.g. local spec validation). CI doesn't need it — it downloads the CLI's
# default version fresh each run. See .github/workflows/api-spec.yml.
openapitools.json

# Superpowers design specs + implementation plans: generated per-session as
# working artifacts, never tracked. Both paths: the skills default to
# docs/superpowers/, and repos whose docs/ is published content use the root.
superpowers/
docs/superpowers/
.superpowers/

# Working notes — investigation records, scratch analysis, session notes. Same
# rationale as docs/superpowers/ above: they earn their keep while a ticket is
# being built and reviewed, then go stale fast (PIDs, bench state, host facts)
# while still reading as authoritative because they are checked in. Durable
# conclusions belong in CLAUDE.md, an ADR or a code comment; the narrative and
# evidence belong on the ticket. Named to match ble-mcp-test.
docs/notes/
docs/investigations/

# Written by sync-preview CI on the preview branch only; read by docker-build
# to embed the merged-PR list into the version string (TRA-851). Never commit
# from a developer branch.
.preview-manifest

# Suite run-shape characterisation artifacts — raw vitest JSON dumps and the
# append-only run log written by frontend/scripts/characterise-suite-runs.mjs.
# Working data: summarise it, put the conclusions somewhere durable, attach the
# evidence to the ticket. Nothing here is committed.
# NOTE: renaming this pattern un-ignores any stale directory still on disk, which
# is how 21 of these were once swept into a PR by `git add -A`. Delete the old
# directory in the same change that renames the pattern.
.suite-runs/
.tra-1167/
